@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Betaling & levering";
    ViewData["TitleEn"] = "Payment & delivery";
}

<div class="wrap section guide-intro">
    <div class="section-head">
        <h1 data-en="Payment &amp; delivery">Betaling &amp; levering</h1>
        <p data-en="Short version: guinea pigs are always picked up in store, accessories can be shipped or picked up, and checkout is a demo payment step, not a real one.">
            Kort fortalt: marsvin afhentes altid i butikken, tilbehør kan
            enten sendes eller afhentes, og betalingstrinnet i kassen er en
            demo, ikke en rigtig betaling.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="section">
    <div class="wrap guide-article">
        <article>
            <h2 data-en="Delivery">Levering</h2>
            <p data-en="Guinea pigs are always picked up in store - a guinea pig can't go in a parcel, and we want to talk through the cage with you before you leave with an animal. That's not something checkout can offer around.">
                Marsvin afhentes altid i butikken - et marsvin kan ikke sendes
                med pakkepost, og vi vil gerne nå at snakke om buret med dig,
                inden du tager af sted med et dyr. Det er ikke noget kassen
                kan tilbyde sig udenom.
            </p>
            <p data-en="Accessories are different: at checkout you choose either pickup in store or shipping to an address you give us there. If your cart mixes a guinea pig with accessories, shipping is still offered for the accessories - the guinea pig itself always needs picking up separately, whichever you choose.">
                Tilbehør er anderledes: i kassen vælger du enten afhentning i
                butikken eller forsendelse til en adresse, du angiver der.
                Blander din kurv et marsvin med tilbehør, kan du stadig vælge
                forsendelse af tilbehøret - marsvinet skal altid afhentes
                separat, uanset hvad du vælger.
            </p>
            <p data-en="An order confirmation shows exactly what was chosen - what to bring and where for a pickup, or the address it's going to for a shipment.">
                En ordrebekræftelse viser præcis hvad der blev valgt - hvad du
                skal medbringe og hvorhen ved afhentning, eller adressen den
                sendes til ved forsendelse.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2 data-en="Shipping: price, delivery time and where it ends up">Fragt: pris, leveringstid og hvor pakken ender</h2>
            <p data-en="Pickup in store is free. Shipping is priced per parcel by weight, and checkout shows the exact price, the expected delivery date and the total for each carrier before you choose.">
                Afhentning i butikken er gratis. Fragt prissættes pr. pakke
                efter vægt, og i kassen ser du den præcise pris, den
                forventede leveringsdato og totalen for hvert fragtselskab,
                inden du vælger.
            </p>
            <table class="cart-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th data-en="Carrier">Fragtselskab</th>
                        <th data-en="Delivered to">Leveres til</th>
                        <th data-en="Delivery time">Leveringstid</th>
                        <th data-en="Up to 1 kg">Op til 1 kg</th>
                        <th data-en="Up to 5 kg">Op til 5 kg</th>
                        <th data-en="Up to 10 kg">Op til 10 kg</th>
                        <th data-en="Up to 20 kg">Op til 20 kg</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    @foreach (var carrier in Enum.GetValues<ShippingCarrier>())
                    {
                        var (minDays, maxDays) = ShippingCalculator.BusinessDays(carrier);
                        <tr>
                            <td>@carrier.DisplayName()</td>
                            @if (carrier.DeliversToParcelShop())
                            {
                                <td data-en="Parcel shop near your address">Pakkeshop nær din adresse</td>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <td data-en="Your door">Din dør</td>
                            }
                            <td data-en="@($"{minDays}-{maxDays} weekdays")">@minDays-@maxDays hverdage</td>
                            @foreach (var grams in new[] { 1_000, 5_000, 10_000, 20_000 })
                            {
                                <td>@ShippingCalculator.Cost(carrier, grams).ToString("N0") kr.</td>
                            }
                        </tr>
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
            <p data-en="A parcel holds at most 20 kg. A heavier order is split into several parcels, each priced on its own weight - checkout tells you how many parcels yours becomes and what it weighs in total. For a parcel shop, the carrier picks the one nearest your address and messages you when the parcel is ready to collect.">
                En pakke rummer højst 20 kg. En tungere ordre deles i flere
                pakker, som hver prissættes efter sin egen vægt - i kassen
                kan du se, hvor mange pakker din ordre bliver til, og hvad
                den vejer i alt. Ved levering til pakkeshop vælger
                fragtselskabet den nærmeste på din adresse og giver besked,
                når pakken kan hentes.
            </p>
            <p data-en="Follow an order under My account: received, being prepared, sent (or ready for pickup), delivered (or picked up).">
                Følg en ordre under Min konto: modtaget, under behandling,
                afsendt (eller klar til afhentning), leveret (eller afhentet).
            </p>
        </article>

        <article>
            <h2 data-en="Payment">Betaling</h2>
            <p data-en="Checkout ends on a demo payment page: it asks for card-shaped details, validates that they're the right shape, and stops there. No card is charged, nothing is sent to a payment provider, and no card details are stored - because there is no real payment integration behind it.">
                Kassen ender på en demo-betalingsside: den beder om
                kortlignende oplysninger, tjekker at de har den rigtige form,
                og stopper der. Der trækkes ikke penge fra noget kort, intet
                sendes til en betalingsudbyder, og ingen kortoplysninger
                gemmes - fordi der ikke er en rigtig betalingsløsning bag den.
            </p>
        </article>

        <div class="callout">
            <h2 data-en="Why not a real payment provider?">Hvorfor ikke en rigtig betalingsudbyder?</h2>
            <p data-en="Taking real payment for animals this shop doesn't actually sell would be fraud, not a school project - a real integration (e.g. Stripe, in test mode) is realistic future work for this project, but this demo step is what stands in for it today.">
                At tage rigtig betaling for dyr, denne butik ikke reelt
                sælger, ville være svindel, ikke et skoleprojekt — en rigtig
                integration (fx Stripe, i testmode) er realistisk fremtidigt
                arbejde for projektet, men dette demo-trin er hvad der står i stedet for det i dag.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
